        <p>lceconstrUction of the olu6 W,ra appended, certified y tbe auditors er apyrovnii by the Committee. which the Committee hoped would be considered satlAfactory by the members. '(Applause). 1 That the members considered the reports sail). rtbetory was at'ested by the unanimity with which ey were received and paned.</p>
        <p>ELECTION OF OFFICERS. • Mr James Lea proposed that Mir John T Brunner. Bart, M. F., be again elected president and accorded Ithellianks of the Club. Mr J Brown seconded,and the motion was carried .with acclamation.</p>
        <p>The -o-tii-e-r—o-fllclals were elected as follows :—Vico- :Presidents, Mes,.rs S Taylor, J P, A R Norman, J P, !R H Posnett, W Ockleston, and George Bellamy; !treasurer, My W A Millinger j secretary,Mr A Riley; !Coremittee W B Beimelow, S T Carruthers, 'EI Chadwick, J Handley, J Jolley. James 6r3en, W Riley, J RawrfriSon, O-Rawlinson, A Ravenseroft, I ,Williams A ft Parr, T Yates ; auditors, Messrs H INV right and T Cooke. Votes of thaults were pas(ed to the last year's- officials, after which the meeting disolved. •</p>
