        <p>Aeliorated in the interval will be manifest froxil an enumeration of some of the most notable changes that have been effected since the cele- bration alluded to. In 1820 slavery was at its height in the British colonies. So long ago asl 1772, ix a suit in the King's Bench, in the case of the slave Somerset, it was established that slavery icould not exist in Great Britain. But it was noti 1833 that the Act for the abolition ofl</p>
