        <p>_ LEOMAS MAYNARD completed the calalogue ofl those who were executed for forgery. There, were no railways, the Stockton and Darlington Bail</p>
        <p>Away, constructed;by STEPHENSON and PEARSE,I lot having been opened until 1825; and the Liver- pool and Manchester Railway, at the opening of Mr. SIISICISSON Was killed, not until 1830. Only a year before, in the year our then future !QusEN was born, the first steamer, the Savannah, the Atlantic. Gas had not yet been sup- to all London, and some of the most impor- of our provincial towns were lighted with ing oil-lamps. The London police did not (commence duty until 1829. The first omnibus in London:started from Paddington to the .of England on Saturday, July 4th 1829. lEighty-one or two years since nobody would have dreamed that in the:lifetime:of any then living one) Aperson would be able to hold immediate commun' Rtion</p>
