        <p>• with another at the other " end" of the earth,l ither with or without wire, and receive an answer at almost the next moment. Rontgen rays andi electric motors were, of course, equally olt of the question. In 1820 APERE had invented his tele- graphic arrangement, employing the magnetic needle and coil, and theTgalvanic battery; but it was not until 1838-9 that Mr. COOKE set up a telegraphic line on the Gre at Western Rail. way, from Paddington to West Drayton. It was only in 1824:that M. DAM:TERRE commenced those curious experiments which,resulted in the wonder- ful art of photography, that has by:no 'means yet . the limits of its power. So common an iiimplemAnt -</p>
