        <p>To-morrow is to be set ape, t as a day of mourn- ng for our late beloved Queen, who will be laid to rest at Frogmore with all the pomp inseparablej from the obsequies of the great. It is the —and we believe the people's—desire that business should be entirely suspended for the day, and we iort all shopkeepers and others to close their inaises and forsake all commercial avocations on an occasion so impressive and saddening. The re- quest is, perhaps, unnecessary, for the majority -,ve a keen appreciation of the fitness of things, ad need no reminder of what is their manifest tuty, but lest there should be a thoughtless few take this opportunity of appealing to them not mar the national expression of sorrow at the (death of Queen Victoria," of blessed memory."</p>
        <p>Aexh,</p>
