      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1901-02-01_WidnesExaminer_art0125" n="art0125">
        <head>ENGLAND'S DANGER. A Returned Soldier's Interesting Statement.</head>
        <p>ENGLAND'S DANGER. A Returned Soldier's Interesting Statement.</p>
        <p>Over a year ago, when the country was depleted of a treat part of the regular army through the war in Jouth Africa, the War Office suddenly called upon those reservists who had passed the age for active service, to rejoin the colours. George Henry Biggins, of 9, Grange Villas, Graoge-street, Hull, who at the time was a sully- man in employment in that city, was amongst those who responded. He served under Sir Charles Warren in South Africa, and was nine months in Mafeking. Some hard campaigning fell to his lot, and though he bears no scar of the battlefield, misfortunes have cerne to him in another shape. An " Eastern Morning News" reporter who called upon him the other day, was certainly able to observe in him nothing but a fine healthy type of the British soldier, yet Mr Biggins owes his present healthy condition exclusively, to Charles Forde's Bile Beans far Biliousness. " I have known the time," he said, " when I used to be strangely overcome by a chilly sensation. It was not altogether cold, for I felt it all over my body, and it seemed to be the result of being altogether run down. I felt languid and too weary and weak to do anything. My joints ached as if I' had rheumatism all over me, and many a time I had difficulty in keeping up with ins' duties. I bezan to suffer from Biliousness, ton, and to experience a nasty sharp pain at my heart. This pain continued to get worse. Whenever I moved at all quickly it com- menced, and I had to go slowly to get ease. So bad did it become at times that I felt convinced I bad heart disease. Of course I tried to get relief, and purchased all kinds of medicines in vain until I tried Chas. Forde's Bile Beans for Biliousness. The result of their use was most satisfactory. I noticed an im- provement aftsr the first few doses, and so went on taking them. They soon fended the biliousness, and from first commencing to take them I have never again felt the pain in the chest. I have suffered fear- fully from biliousness, and am very grateful indeed to the Proprietors of Chas. Forde's Bile Beans. Theyl have now completely cured me, and lam frequently, recommending them to persons I find suffering as I did. While at Gosport I gave some to a gunner, and his mother-in-law derived great benefit from them. Oalyi the other night my little daughter was quite out of sorts and I gave her half a Bean. The next day she was all; right again. I can tell you, my f smily,both young and; old, have used them with marvellous results." Where. ever Charles Ferde's Bile Beans for Biliousness are used, marvellous results follow4For colds and chills, indiges- tion, antemia dizziness, liver and kidney disorders, con- stipation, debility, headache, nervousness, female ail- ments, rheumatism, and as a preventative of influeoza the 7 are unequalled. Purely vegetable in eornoositioh, their use is followed not mvely by tertaperary Improve- ment, hut by permanent cure. All chemists stock them, or you may obtain direct from the Bile Bean Manu- facturing Co., 119,London Wall,London,E .0 ~by sending prices, one and three half-pence or two and nine. They have been instrumental in restoring to health scores of Private Biggins. lone gallant defenders, as they did</p>
