        <p>)nclusion he said that he should be surprised if the , _Amy went very far before something was done to wards a satisfactory settlement. He believed the day was coming, assure as he stood on that platform, when the drink evil would disappear. (Applause). During the evening recitations, songs, and duets were, zontributed by Miss Morrell, Miss M. D. Ross, Messrs. G. Gough, R. Cook and Dunn. An interesting feature of the proceedings was the presentation of an emblem tol tro. J. Garner and certificates of merit to Bros. E. atlewood and E. Edwards. The recipients brief! Ikno wledged the gifts. A comprehensive vote of thanks having been accorddi lito the chairman, artistes, and all who had assisted, ' proceedings were'brought to a close with the singing " God save the King.' by</p>
