        <p>Bro A Bennett, the high chief ruler of the Order of Rechabites, then delivered an address, and at the outset said he heartily concurred in the sentiments which bad been expressed with reference to the late beloved Queen. ffe proceeded to refer to the obedience of the Rechabites s related in the 35.',h chapter of the book of Jeremiah td stated that the motives which animated the sons of hmse of the Rechabttes were those of the order ofi abltes to-day. He showed that the foundation of alatate' -</p>
