        <p>Swinton don't seem to like wet'weather at all, and, • Lion's coat has been very much besmeared in the last; encounters, S. Helene trampled all over it a week go last Saturday, while poor despised Wigan left al mark on Saturday. The leaders of the league actually; could not defeat the wooden-spoonists at Swinton, which says a lot for the "do wet" being a great leveller.; Fortunately for the Lions the Oldham men succumbed' • the rushes of the Rangers at Broughton. and they are a clear three points in arrear. Runcorn have [climbed to smond place by virtue of a win over Salford, land will very likely cause trouble as Sviintou have yet • visit the banks of the Irwell.</p>
