        <p>The Swinton v. Oldham -match having been ordered be replayed, the game on January 12 has been struck tt of the above table.</p>
        <p>Owing to the mourning order and the feeling of . ttion, them will be no football matches played to vrow. Warrington should have journed to Oldham' that licking is postponed for the time being. Pro. AS7 the match will have to be played on some mid- week day.</p>
        <p>The next match is also away, Warrington playing Leigh at Leigh. The Mather-laners have been doing fairly well of late and may be relied upon to give War- rington a stiff game. Last season we won at Leigh in handsome fashion, Fish scoring three brilliant tries, and is after haviag lost at Wilderspool to the same club. is imperative that Warrington should" buck-up," oi Ire will be a poor record to show at the season's end. point dropped on Saturday hot will be badly:wanted 4. In fact it was badly wanted a week since, for a 4 win would have lifted Warrington two rungs up the ladder, and above Barrow too.</p>
        <p>It is clear now that Warrington will have to rely on (practically a local team for the cup ties, for to-day is last day for registering cup-tie players, and War. ton hive not secured any "new un3" this week. We it to be able to make a good show with the talent in town if all the men are available.</p>
        <p>C RAWFORD'S CERAM CRACKERS, CRISP AND r`REAMY</p>
        <p>A New Dietary for Deserving Inmates. A meeting of thispoard was held in the Board Room at the Workhouse on Wednesday morning. Mr A J Jolley presided andithere were also present :—Mrs Clay, Mrs Edelsten, Rev J H Riddette, Messrs S Davies, William Hickman, J Billinge, T H Ashcroft, T B Malkiii,William Houghton, T Halt in, J Ball, A Jolley, J Clarke, Henry Thornton, G Piiling,l Johnson, A. Brook, with J Cd Suttonclerk), S Sutton (assistant clerk), C H War) (master),and A Wright(Superintendent Padgate Schools RESIGNATION OF A NURSE. The CLERK reported that the resignation of Nurse leeping had been received and accepted. ACKNOWLEDGMENT. The DUSTER rep )rted that he had received gifts ?apers, magazines &amp;c. for the inmates from Messrs T H Ashcroft, E L Bent and Fryer. NEW DIETARY TABLES. WILL THE cosr BE INCREASED ? The Medical Officer at a meeting of the House Com-, mittee on January 25h, verbally stated that he hadl oproved of the seheme of the new dietaries as suggested the sub-committee, and had also drawn up new 3taries for the sick in accordance with the new order if the L:cal Government Board, dated October 1900. The committee recommended that it was desirable that the grouping of the inmates into classes for the purposes (of diet should be entrusted to the Master, to be carried out under the general control of the House Committee' so should be empowered to give such directions,general ,e special, as might be lawfully given by the Guardians in any case in which there was doubt as to the interpre- tation of the general order, or for the directions of the Guardians, the Master should act as be might deem, best, pending the decision of the House Committee, to; whom he should report such case at the next meeting, - view of the terms of Article 111., section 2, it was sirabli3 that the existing regulations permitting giflal certain classes of inmates should be rescinded so - they were incompatible therewith, and that a I egulation absolutely prohibitiag the introduction into; the Workhouse by any person of any gifts of liquor orl food for the use of any inmate shoold be adopted. It, was further desirable that such a regulation should be elated, and copies thereof, with an intimation of the Isequences of any infraction of the rule,be distributed lamongst those persons who habitually visited the Work- house, including the ladies who worked in connection with the Brabazon scheme. The CLERIC read some correspondence on the same ibject from which it appeared that at a meeting of •esentatives of the three Liverpool Boards of Guar- , (West Derby, Toxteth Park and Liverpool) it was animously decided to ask the Local Government lard to sanction the postponement for six months ati ket Of the introduction et the Workhouse Dietaries Irder. . -</p>
