        <p>MISCELLANCotTS.—Jehn Smith, for having used obscene language at Stockton Heath on December Bth, was tined in the costs. —A similar penalty was meted out to John Howard for having no light on his lorry on the 23th December—For allowing seven heifers to stray at Lowerl IWhitley on the 22nd December. John H Clark was fined In ;the aosts.--Samuel Robert Theodore. who bad no light on his i 'bicycle at 12.30 a.m, on the 13th January. was also fined in the costs.— George LongshAw Was fined in the costs for keep- ing a dog without a licence. I I ---</p>
        <p>Runcorn Petty Sessions. idownaar,—Before Messrs, W. Timmins (presiding) and H. Imison. CA3M—Matthias ?ye. Kinv-street, was fined 5s costs for using obscene language.- -William Riley, sailor, of Staiybridge for b ling drunk in Percival-lane, We+ fined 5s a Howard, of Brunswick-street. was also fined 101 for :ennees: Joseph Bolland. Fryer-ctreet, was fined WI Booth: of 52 Akhridge-street. was granted a cer- f exemption under the Vaccination Act, in respect' Id born 25th November. His objection was that children was at prese at suffering from the evi COAL " Oaw,</p>
