        <head>WOMAN'S AFFLICTIONS.</head>
        <p>WOMAN'S AFFLICTIONS.</p>
        <p>Suspension of Business. Satnrday being arranged for the funeral of Her</p>
        <p>late most Gracious Majesty the Queen, the Mast</p>
        <p>Bakers of Warrington a-t a meeting held on Wed- nesday, unanimously decided not to bake or deliver bread on that day. Generally speaking, the rail- way traffic on Saturday will be conducted as on, Sundays. There will be a general closing of goodsi stations, locomotive and carriage works, and cleri- cal offices over the country. A meeting of the War-, rington Hairdressers was held in Mr Oldfield's shop.l Bewsey-street, on Tuesday night, when it was deci- ded to close from 11.30 to 230 on the day of the Queen's funeral. A special meeting of the licensed victuallers of Warrington and district was held on Tuesday, p sided over by Councillor Shillcoek. It was deck to close all houses in Warrington and district Saturday from 11 a.m. until 5 p.m.</p>
