        <p>The services at this church were of a character befit- ting t' lam</p>
        <p>the solemnity of the occasion. Special psalms and ins were sung and special lessons read. The Vicar H G Hollingworth)preached at each of the services. tn thejmorning he tack for his tExt the worda"Have pity ipon me, have pity upon me, oye my friends ; for the iand of God hath touched me." Job xis. 21. He said the hand of God bad indeed touched them. They mourn,- alruled</p>
