        <p>RUNCORN RURAL DISTRICT, f COUNCIL. BP. Knowles, .T.P., presided over the usual fort ,nightly meeting of the above Council on Tuesday last, there were also present :—Messrs Jones-Parry, 8 Wood- ward, J Stokes. T Wright, C E .Linaker. T Baxter, T Lewis. W Fletcher, George Pilli.g. P Leather, J Edwards, E Otsrk, J Mounfield, J Moseley Williams, E Brether- tor, T Darlington. with Mr George F Amhton (clerk), Mr W E Fr-nigh (deputy clerk), Messrs Diggle and Swinton (auroevora),M, James Farrington (inspector), and Dr J Adams (medical officer of health). LOCAL RUCTIONS. The Local Government Board forwarded copies of the general order they had issued altering the dates far the ainceedings at elections of Rural District Councillors in (the present year. -On the motion of Mr Woodward. seconded by Mr inaker,the Council akin decided to apply to the County Jouncil that the election take place on Saturday, March PROPOSED ALTERATION.' IN NORLEY LANE. Mr. Charles T Geri% Estate Office, Delarnere House, Torthwich, forwarded plans of the alterations and ins— :o...merits which Mr Charles Bell, ot Norley, proposed o make in Norlev-lane. Mr Bell proposed to make these alterations entiielv at his own cost., and he booed they would meet with-the approval of the Council. The mater was deletated to the consideration of a small committee, which will input and report to the Council. THE CANAL BOATI ACT. Mr. James Farrington, inopec'or under the Canal Boats Acts. tenorted that during the year ended 31st December 1900, twenty-two boats were inspected whilst passisg through the Council'. District,and the condition of the whole of such boats was found to be very satis- factory, especially those boats which were without f,-males on board. No eases ot infectious diseases were !met with. The report was received as satisfactory. •</p>
